diagnosis_text:
A thorough seven-layer investigation found no fault. The reported symptom — hosts on 10.5.0.x and 10.6.0.x unable to reach their gateways 10.5.0.254 and 10.6.0.254 — could not be reproduced. Direct ICMP probes from pc1 (10.5.0.1) to 10.5.0.254 and from pc3 (10.6.0.3) to 10.6.0.254 both returned 0% packet loss with sub-millisecond RTTs. Cross-subnet reachability (e.g., 10.5.0.x hosts reaching 172.16.10.x peers) also succeeds at 0% loss, which is only possible when the gateway is forwarding correctly. The gateway interfaces br_v5 (10.5.0.254/24) and br_v6 (10.6.0.254/24) on sshswitch are UP, bound to the correct VLAN-subinterface bridges (eth0.5/eth0.6 from switch4, bond0.5/bond0.6 from router17), and actively carrying traffic per /proc/net/dev counters. OSPF is fully converged across all nine routers (18 routes each, all adjacencies Full), link-layer counters show zero errors and zero carrier changes on every interface, and no ACL rules, TC shaping, duplicate MACs, resource pressure, or syslog entries indicative of any fault were found. The helpdesk report references a "reload earlier," but none of the mechanism indicators required to substantiate a past fault — flap scripts, carrier-change history, syslog alerts, or stale/missing bridge entries — are present. The claim is unconfirmed and the network is currently fully operational. Root cause: no anomaly exists; the ticket cannot be substantiated by direct evidence.
